{
  "$format": "janus-conformance-case/1",
  "id": "live/recorded-shape",
  "category": "live",
  "title": "A provider's own tests, naming only the operation, record the sample provider's variance as one shape: an entry per status, selected by the operation.",
  "covers": [
    "verification.observe.frame",
    "verification.finish-recording.writes-shape"
  ],
  "why": "behavioural spec 'observe' and 'finish-recording' (ADR 0086), against the real engine: the operation becomes each entry's selector, with the status the engine writes into it, the body's octets are decoded as the JSON they are labelled as, and the engine's host writes the shape. These are the answers the sample provider gives (samples/order-service), and engine/kernel/tests/provider_shape_by_operation.rs checks this shape against that provider's consumer pact: it is matched by the operation and finds the CANCELLED status the consumer never tested (staged plan S4.1's exit).",
